B.a90=A.a(s(["Book transit buses and campgrounds months ahead.","Eielson Visitor Center (mile 66) has the classic Denali view.","Cell service ends at the park entrance \u2014 download maps first."]),t.s)
B.Wz=new A.el("denali","Denali National Park","Parks","Interior",63.1148,-151.1926,"\ud83c\udfd4\ufe0f","North America's tallest peak and six million wild acres.",'Home of 20,310-ft Denali, the park is crossed by a single 92-mile road plied by transit buses. Grizzlies, caribou, Dall sheep, moose, and wolves \u2014 the "Big Five" \u2014 are all regularly spotted from the road. Only 30% of visitors see the mountain itself; clear mornings are your best shot.',"June \u2013 early September",4.9,B.a90)
B.a2x=A.a(s(["The 8-hour Northwestern Fjord cruise beats the half-day trips.","Hike the Harding Icefield Trail for a top-of-the-world view (strenuous, 8+ mi)."]),t.s)
B.Wr=new A.el("kenai-fjords","Kenai Fjords National Park","Parks","Southcentral",59.9226,-149.65,"\ud83d\udc0b","Tidewater glaciers, orcas, and puffins out of Seward.","The Harding Icefield spills 38 glaciers toward the Gulf of Alaska. Day cruises from Seward thread past calving tidewater glaciers, humpbacks, orcas, sea otters, and bird rookeries. Exit Glacier is the only road-accessible corner of the park.","May \u2013 September",4.9,B.a2x)
B.a1Q=A.a(s(["Access is via guided tour only \u2014 book ahead in summer.","The Glenn Highway drive there is a National Scenic Byway; budget photo stops."]),t.s)
B.Wi=new A.el("matanuska","Matanuska Glacier","Glaciers","Southcentral",61.7011,-147.7503,"\ud83e\uddca","Walk on a 27-mile river of ice, two hours from Anchorage.","The largest road-accessible glacier in the U.S., reached from a turnoff at Glenn Highway mile 102. Guided treks cross blue ice fins, moulins, and meltwater pools; winter tours explore frozen caves lit electric blue.","Year-round (guided)",4.8,B.a1Q)
B.aaR=A.a(s(["Photo Point trail at sunrise beats the midday cruise-ship crowds."]),t.s)
B.Ws=new A.el("mendenhall","Mendenhall Glacier","Glaciers","Southeast",58.4366,-134.5453,"\u2744\ufe0f","Juneau's drive-up glacier with a thundering waterfall neighbor.","Thirteen miles from downtown Juneau, Mendenhall calves into its own lake beside 377-ft Nugget Falls. The flat 2-mile round-trip Nugget Falls trail is the best effort-to-reward walk in Southeast. Black bears fish the creek in late summer.","May \u2013 September",4.7,B.aaR)
B.Wj=new A.el("exit-glacier","Exit Glacier","Glaciers","Southcentral",60.1867,-149.6319,"\ud83e\udded","Seward's walk-to glacier, with year markers tracking its retreat.","The only drive-up corner of Kenai Fjords NP. An easy 1-mile loop reaches glacier overlooks, passing signs marking where the ice stood each decade \u2014 a sobering, fascinating timeline. Strong hikers continue up the Harding Icefield Trail.","May \u2013 October",4.6,B.k)
B.a6e=A.a(s(["The Russian River confluence is combat fishing at its finest in July.","Check ADF&G emergency orders before every trip \u2014 regs change weekly."]),t.s)
B.Wl=new A.el("kenai-river","Kenai River","Fishing","Southcentral",60.5439,-150.7886,"\ud83c\udfa3","World-famous salmon water \u2014 kings, reds, silvers, and giant rainbows.","Alaska's most famous fishery. Sockeye floods arrive in June and July, silvers run through fall, and the trophy rainbow trout fishery below Skilak Lake is world-class. Drift boats, bank fishing, and guided trips all produce.","June \u2013 October",4.8,B.a6e)
B.aaY=A.a(s(["Full-day charters reach better halibut grounds than half-day trips.","Eagles on the beach at low tide are an event in themselves."]),t.s)
B.Wn=new A.el("homer","Homer Spit","Fishing","Southcentral",59.6028,-151.4178,"\ud83d\udea4","Halibut capital of the world, at the end of the road.","A 4.5-mile gravel spit jutting into Kachemak Bay, lined with charter docks, fish shacks, art galleries, and the Salty Dawg Saloon. Halibut charters run daily in season; across the bay, water taxis open up Kachemak Bay State Park's trails and coves.","May \u2013 September",4.7,B.aaY)
B.Wm=new A.el("ship-creek","Ship Creek","Fishing","Southcentral",61.2272,-149.8694,"\ud83d\udc1f","Catch a king salmon downtown, ten minutes from your hotel.","The only urban king salmon fishery of its kind \u2014 kings June, silvers August, with downtown Anchorage towers in the background. Rental rods and tackle shops sit streamside; the bore tide mudflats are dangerous, so fish from the bank areas.","June \u2013 September",4.3,B.k)
B.a6v=A.a(s(["Reed Lakes trail is the Talkeetnas' showpiece \u2014 turquoise lakes and boulder fields.","The pass road closes beyond Independence Mine in winter."]),t.s)
B.Wh=new A.el("hatcher","Hatcher Pass","Hiking","Southcentral",61.7706,-149.3028,"\u26f0\ufe0f","Alpine tundra, gold-mine ruins, and berry picking above the Mat-Su.","A high mountain pass through the Talkeetnas with the historic Independence Mine ruins at its heart. Summer means alpine hikes (Gold Cord Lake, April Bowl, Reed Lakes) and blueberries; winter brings backcountry skiing and sledding.","July \u2013 September; winter for skiing",4.8,B.a6v)
B.a6u=A.a(s(["Go before 10 AM or take the shoulder-season window for parking.","Moose browse the lower trail constantly \u2014 give them room."]),t.s)
B.Wk=new A.el("flattop","Flattop Mountain","Hiking","Southcentral",61.1042,-149.6837,"\ud83e\udd7e","Alaska's most-climbed peak, 30 minutes from downtown Anchorage.","A 1.5-mile, 1,300-ft scramble from Glen Alps trailhead to a flat summit with views from Denali to the Aleutians on a clear day. The classic summer-solstice sunset hike for locals. The final pitch is a hands-on rock scramble.","June \u2013 September",4.5,B.a6u)
B.a24=A.a(s(["Ford Eagle River early morning when glacial melt is lowest."]),t.s)
B.Wo=new A.el("crow-pass","Crow Pass Trail","Hiking","Southcentral",61.0306,-149.1217,"\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f","The Chugach's premier point-to-point: glaciers, gorge, and a river ford.","A 21-mile traverse from Girdwood to the Eagle River Nature Center along the historic Iditarod route \u2014 waterfalls, Raven Glacier, mining relics, and a genuine glacial river ford. Done as an overnight or a long single day by fit hikers.","July \u2013 early September",4.8,B.a24)
B.a9E=A.a(s(["Day trips sell out nearly a year out \u2014 book early.","Bear school at the ranger station is mandatory on arrival."]),t.s)
B.Ww=new A.el("katmai","Katmai \u2013 Brooks Falls","Wildlife","Southwest",58.555,-155.7775,"\ud83d\udc3b","The famous waterfall where brown bears snatch leaping salmon.","Every July, dozens of brown bears crowd Brooks Falls to catch sockeye mid-air \u2014 the scene from every Alaska documentary. Reached by floatplane from King Salmon; viewing platforms put you safely within yards of thousand-pound fishermen.","July; September for fat-bear season",4.9,B.a9E)
B.Wp=new A.el("kodiak","Kodiak Island","Wildlife","Southwest",57.79,-152.4072,"\ud83e\udd85","Emerald island of giant bears and epic roadside fishing.","The Kodiak brown bear \u2014 the largest in the world \u2014 shares this lush island with a major fishing fleet and road-accessible salmon streams. Floatplane bear-viewing at Frazer Lake, surfcasting for silvers, and the Kodiak NWR visitor center fill an itinerary fast.","June \u2013 September",4.7,B.k)
B.Wv=new A.el("aialik","St. Paul \u2013 Pribilof Islands","Wildlife","Bering Sea",57.1264,-170.2764,"\ud83d\udc26","The Gal\xe1pagos of the north \u2014 fur seals and a million seabirds.","Way out in the Bering Sea, the Pribilofs host the world's largest northern fur seal rookeries and legendary birding \u2014 puffins, auklets, and Asian vagrants that draw listers from everywhere. Remote, foggy, unforgettable.","June \u2013 August",4.6,B.k)
B.a5o=A.a(s(["Check the UAF Geophysical Institute forecast; aim for Kp 3+.","Peak display window is 10 PM \u2013 2 AM."]),t.s)
B.Wx=new A.el("murphy-dome","Murphy Dome","Aurora","Interior",64.9536,-148.3565,"\ud83c\udf0c","Fairbanks' favorite aurora hill, above the fog and the light dome.","A 2,930-ft dome 25 minutes from Fairbanks with 360\xb0 horizons \u2014 the go-to aurora perch for locals. Directly under the auroral oval, Fairbanks sees lights on 4 of 5 clear winter nights. Bring arctic layers; you'll be standing still at -20\xb0F.","late August \u2013 mid April",4.7,B.a5o)
B.aak=A.a(s(["Your hair will freeze into sculptures at -20\xb0F. That's the photo."]),t.s)
B.Wy=new A.el("chena","Chena Hot Springs","Hot Springs","Interior",65.0539,-146.0556,"\u2668\ufe0f","Soak in 106\xb0F rock pools while the aurora burns overhead.","Sixty miles up the Chena Hot Springs Road from Fairbanks, the resort's outdoor rock lake steams at 106\xb0F year-round. Add the Aurora Ice Museum (carved ice bar, -7\xb0F inside) and late-night aurora wake-up calls and you have the Interior's classic winter stop.","Year-round; winter for aurora soaks",4.6,B.aak)
B.a1M=A.a(s(["Pay for the glacier landing. Nobody regrets it.","The river bluff behind town frames Denali on clear evenings."]),t.s)
B.WA=new A.el("talkeetna","Talkeetna","Towns","Interior",62.3209,-150.1066,"\ud83d\udee9\ufe0f","Quirky climber town with the best Denali flightseeing in Alaska.","The staging town for Denali expeditions, all log cabins, roadhouse pie, and bush planes. Flightseeing trips circle the Alaska Range and land on the Ruth Glacier \u2014 twenty minutes of silence inside a mile-deep granite amphitheater.","May \u2013 September",4.7,B.a1M)
B.a4p=A.a(s(["Time the bore tide at Beluga Point \u2014 surfers ride a wave up the Arm."]),t.s)
B.Wu=new A.el("girdwood","Girdwood & Alyeska","Towns","Southcentral",60.962,-149.1101,"\ud83d\udea1","Rainforest ski town with a tram, hand pies, and hanging glaciers.","Forty minutes from Anchorage along Turnagain Arm, Girdwood pairs Alyeska Resort's aerial tram and ski terrain with lush hemlock trails like Winner Creek. The Turnagain Arm drive there \u2014 bore tides, beluga whales, Dall sheep on the cliffs \u2014 is itself a hot spot.","Year-round",4.7,B.a4p)
B.Wq=new A.el("valdez","Valdez & Thompson Pass","Towns","Southcentral",61.1308,-146.3483,"\ud83c\udfc2","Waterfall-lined fjord town beneath Alaska's snowiest pass.","The Richardson Highway drops through Keystone Canyon's curtain waterfalls into a fjord ringed by peaks. Summer brings pink salmon runs, sea kayaking to Columbia Glacier; winter, Thompson Pass's 700+ inches of snow makes it heli-ski country.","June \u2013 September; March for snow",4.6,B.k)
B.Wt=new A.el("utqiagvik","Utqia\u0121vik (Barrow)","Towns","Arctic",71.2906,-156.7886,"\ud83e\uddca","The top of America \u2014 midnight sun, polar bears, I\xf1upiat culture.","The northernmost town in the U.S., where the sun doesn't set for 80 days of summer or rise for 65 days of winter. Visit for I\xf1upiat heritage, whale-bone arches on the Arctic Ocean beach, and fall polar bear viewing near Point Barrow.","June \u2013 August; October for polar bears",4.4,B.k)
