B.Ul=new A.K(52,"Big Lake / Houston","\u26fd",61.628,-149.826,"A cluster of gas stations, motels, and restaurants near the turnoff for Big Lake, one of the Mat-Su Valley's most popular boating and fishing lakes. A good last stop for fuel before the highway leaves the bulk of the valley's development behind.","Food")
B.Vs=new A.K(69,"Willow","\u26fd",61.7544,-150.0461,"Small community that briefly served as the planned site of Alaska's capital in a 1976 ballot measure that was never funded. Today it's the ceremonial restart point of the Iditarod Trail Sled Dog Race and offers fuel, lodging, and access to the Willow Creek State Recreation Area.","Fuel")
B.Sv=new A.K(96,"Montana Creek","\ud83c\udfa3",62.296,-150.068,"A popular roadside spot where Montana Creek crosses the highway, known for strong runs of king, silver, and pink salmon. Several private campgrounds and fishing guide outfits cluster around the bridge during summer salmon season.","Camp Ground")
B.TV=new A.K(115,"Trapper Creek","\u26fd",62.314,-150.198,"A rural crossroads community at the junction with the Petersville Road, which heads west toward old gold-mining country and views of the Alaska Range. Trapper Creek has fuel, lodging, and a public library serving the surrounding homestead area.","Fuel")
B.VZ=new A.K(134.5,"K'esugi Ken Campground","\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f",62.591,-150.23,"The flagship campground of Denali State Park, opened in 2017 with paved RV and walk-in sites, public-use cabins, and an interpretive pavilion. A network of trails climbs onto the K'esugi Ridge alpine tundra, with some of the best non-park views of Denali on the entire highway.","Camp Ground")
B.VH=new A.K(135.2,"South Denali Viewpoint","\u26f0\ufe0f",62.604,-150.233,"A signed pullout in Denali State Park offering one of the closest unobstructed views of Denali (20,310 ft) accessible from the road, weather permitting. On clear days the entire south face of the Alaska Range, including the Tokositna and Ruth Glacier valleys, dominates the western horizon.","Pull Off / Rest Area")
B.UR=new A.K(147,"Byers Lake Campground","\ud83c\udfd5\ufe0f",62.7,-150.027,"A forested Denali State Park campground on the shore of Byers Lake, with a 4.8-mile loop trail circling the lake through spruce and birch forest. Canoeing and lake-trout fishing are popular, and on clear days the lake reflects Denali to the northwest.","Camp Ground")
B.V5=new A.K(188,"Hurricane Gulch Bridge","\u26f0\ufe0f",63.021,-149.597,"A dramatic steel arch bridge spanning a 260-foot-deep gorge cut by Hurricane Creek, one of the highest bridges in Alaska. The pullouts at either end give views down into the gulch and west toward the Alaska Range foothills.","Pull Off / Rest Area")
B.Sy=new A.K(210,"Cantwell (Denali Highway Junction)","\ud83d\udd00",63.392,-148.95,"A small Athabascan community at the eastern end of the Denali Highway, which heads 134 miles east to Paxson through remote tundra and mountain scenery. Cantwell has fuel, lodging, and is the last services before the climb toward Denali National Park.","Fuel")
B.TS=new A.K(237.4,"Denali National Park Entrance","\ud83e\udd8c",63.7284,-148.8866,"Main entrance to Denali National Park and Preserve, home to grizzly bears, caribou, moose, wolves, and Dall sheep across 6 million acres of taiga and tundra. The park visitor center, sled dog kennels, and the start of the restricted-access park road are all near this junction.","Visitor Center")
B.Un=new A.K(238,"Nenana Canyon","\u26fd",63.735,-148.895,'The dense strip of hotels, restaurants, and rafting outfitters just north of the park entrance, nicknamed "Glitter Gulch," sits above the Nenana River\'s canyon. A rest area at the river bridge is a good spot to watch outfitters launch Class III-IV whitewater rafting trips through the gorge.',"Food")
B.UU=new A.K(248.7,"Healy","\ud83c\udffa",63.8714,-148.9683,"Home to the Usibelli Coal Mine, Alaska's only operating commercial coal mine, founded in 1943 and still supplying interior power plants. Healy has year-round fuel, groceries, and lodging, serving as a quieter alternative base for visiting Denali.","Fuel")
B.TW=new A.K(35,"Glenn-Parks Interchange","\ud83d\udd00",61.5535,-149.2473,"A highway junction \u2014 junction of glenn and parks highways.","Scenic Feature / Attraction")
B.TK=new A.K(42.2,"Wasilla","\ud83d\udccd",61.5814,-149.4492,"A community along the Parks Highway \u2014 junction with knik-goose bay road.","Scenic Feature / Attraction")
